-- src:6296 | 8. Order 9, Rule 24 applies in relation to the taking of evidence for arbitral proceedings under Article 27 of the Model Law as it applies for the purpose of proceedings in the Court.
@ref O 48 r 8 (src:6296)
GIVEN `the evidence is taken for arbitral proceedings under Article 27 of the Model Law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 48 r 8 Order 9, Rule 24 applies to the taking of the evidence` MEANS
    IF `the evidence is taken for arbitral proceedings under Article 27 of the Model Law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule speaks of "the taking of evidence for arbitral proceedings under Article 27 of the Model Law"
